      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.84,
      "end_seconds": 4.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.46,
      "end_seconds": 9.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "that's fine, sit down tell me why you came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.71,
      "end_seconds": 18.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "well, it's yellow eyes i thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.49,
      "end_seconds": 40.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Right, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.37,
      "end_seconds": 48.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "around five days... no wait, um, it's more like two days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.35,
      "end_seconds": 50.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "I see, go ahead"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.16,
      "end_seconds": 54.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "And itching all over, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.37,
      "end_seconds": 70.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Has there been any swelling of the tummy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.75,
      "end_seconds": 76.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "well, not that I've noticed, no swelling of the tummy"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.16,
      "end_seconds": 81.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "okay, have you noticed fever or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.89,
      "end_seconds": 86.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "let me think, none of those, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.55,
      "end_seconds": 89.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.16,
      "end_seconds": 92.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "no, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.46,
      "end_seconds": 98.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.06,
      "end_seconds": 104.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "I mean, no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.46,
      "end_seconds": 108.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "okay, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.11,
      "end_seconds": 113.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.55,
      "end_seconds": 130.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.52,
      "end_seconds": 133.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "My son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.85,
      "end_seconds": 137.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.22,
      "end_seconds": 159.34,
      "duration_seconds": 20.12,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I hardly move around during the day. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.26,
      "end_seconds": 180.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.96,
      "end_seconds": 191.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "I've had diabetes, yes sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit my neighbour said I should get it looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.98,
      "end_seconds": 198.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.31,
      "end_seconds": 204.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "I'm on gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.18,
      "end_seconds": 211.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.92,
      "end_seconds": 213.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.34,
      "end_seconds": 217.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.81,
      "end_seconds": 233.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "The whites of your eyes are yellow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.37,
      "end_seconds": 237.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.39,
      "end_seconds": 250.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Liver edge is just palpable and mildly tender"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.89,
      "end_seconds": 273.66,
      "duration_seconds": 17.77,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Putting it it all together, I'd lean towards jaundice with a cause we still need to find. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.14,
      "end_seconds": 279.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.67,
      "end_seconds": 305.02,
      "duration_seconds": 24.35,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's jaundice with a cause we still need to find, and we'll know more once the an ultrasound of the abdomen is back. So, to recap quickly. You've had yellow eyes for two days, and no black stools or swelling of the tummy"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.83,
      "end_seconds": 307.53,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.23,
      "end_seconds": 320.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "I think an ultrasound of the abdomen makes sense here, for jaundice. I want a hepatitis screen done, that's for jaundice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.32,
      "end_seconds": 322.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.27,
      "end_seconds": 348.62,
      "duration_seconds": 24.35,
      "text": "Please avoid alcohol completely and don't take any painkillers except paracetamol, and not much of that. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. I'm gonna send a referral to a liver specialist. Come back after the results are back. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.32,
      "end_seconds": 353.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "great, thank you for your help"
    }
  ]
}